Here’s a concise summary of the video:

The video highlights a significant security risk with AI browsing tools. When using tools like ChaggyPTs, you’re essentially giving your AI assistant permission to freely browse the web, opening it up to “prompt injection attacks.” These attacks trick the AI into performing unintended actions by feeding it instructions from websites. To protect yourself, the video recommends using three key prompts: 1) Limit the AI’s actions to the original task, 2) Require a full plan approval before complex actions, and 3) Flag and reject any instructions found in web content. Ignoring these boundaries can lead to your AI being manipulated and potentially exposing sensitive information.

