Here’s a concise summary of the video transcription:

The video highlights the importance of using “chain of thought prompting” with ChatGPT to get better results. Simply asking ChatGPT a broad question won’t work. Instead, break down large tasks into smaller, step-by-step instructions, mimicking your own thought process. This technique, similar to cognitive behavioral therapy, helps ChatGPT understand and respond more effectively. Essentially, you’re teaching it to think like you, leading to more focused and productive outputs. Don’t treat ChatGPT as a muse; treat it like a middle manager needing a clear process to deliver quality results.

